  "segments": [
    {
      "start": 0.0,
      "end": 4.96,
      "text": "Looking at the second column of this graphic, your next priority is to build your skills."
    },
    {
      "start": 5.64,
      "end": 10.52,
      "text": "This means you need to learn how to write, build, solve problems, and work directly with"
    },
    {
      "start": 10.52,
      "end": 10.98,
      "text": "other people."
    },
    {
      "start": 11.48,
      "end": 16.08,
      "text": "You also have to practice listening actively and communicating your ideas clearly."
    },
    {
      "start": 16.98,
      "end": 21.34,
      "text": "These broad abilities serve as the necessary baseline tools you use to interact with the"
    },
    {
      "start": 21.34,
      "end": 25.5,
      "text": "world and execute tasks, laying the groundwork for more complex thought."
    },
    {
      "start": 26.2,
      "end": 29.56,
      "text": "Once those basics are in place, you have to practice thinking critically."
    },
    {
      "start": 30.36,
      "end": 34.24,
      "text": "The first mechanical step of that process is to question the claims you hear."
    },
    {
      "start": 34.98,
      "end": 37.52,
      "text": "Next, you have to carefully weigh the available evidence."
    },
    {
      "start": 38.46,
      "end": 41.4,
      "text": "Finally, you take what you know to make informed decisions."
    },
    {
      "start": 42.2,
      "end": 46.94,
      "text": "Breaking the process down into these three sequential, actionable steps turns critical"
    },
    {
      "start": 46.94,
      "end": 52.7,
      "text": "thinking from an abstract idea into a concrete, usable mechanism for evaluating reality."
    },
    {
      "start": 53.52,
      "end": 55.86,
      "text": "School is where you get to build what you bring to the work."
    }
  ],
